    "description": {
      "value": "<p><em>Wondrous Item, Uncommon</em></p><p>A <em>Hag Eye</em> has 3 charges. While wearing or holding it, you can expend 1 charge to cast @UUID[Compendium.dnd5e.spells24.Item.phbsplDarkvision]{Darkvision} (targeting yourself only) or @UUID[Compendium.dnd5e.spells24.Item.phbsplSeeInvisib]{See Invisibility} from it. The <em>Hag Eye</em> regains all expended charges daily at dawn.</p><p><strong>Coven Sensor.</strong> A <em>Hag Eye</em> is usually handed to one of a hag’s minions to keep and carry. As a Magic action, a hag of the coven that made the eye can see what the eye sees, as long as the hag and the eye are on the same plane of existence. This lasts as long as the hag maintains Concentration, and several hags of the coven can look through the eye at the same time.</p><p><strong>Creating a Hag Eye.</strong> Only a hag coven can make this item, which is a real eye coated in varnish and often set into a pendant or another wearable item. A coven can have only one <em>Hag Eye</em> at a time. Making a new one requires all three members of the coven to perform a special rite lasting 1 hour, which they can’t perform if any of them has the &amp;Reference[Incapacitated apply=false] condition. If the hags take any other actions during the rite, it fails and ends.</p>",
